{"Title":"An Act to assess school integration within the Metropolitan Council for Educational Opportunity (METCO) program","BillNumber":"H4408","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J14","Name":"Joint Committee on Education","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14","ResponseDate":"2024-02-02T09:16:51.64"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"C_T1","Name":"Chynah Tyler","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/C_T1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-13T10:48:45.87"},{"Id":"V_H1","Name":"Vanna Howard","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/V_H1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-14T12:17:25.0166667"},{"Id":"MMD1","Name":"Michelle M. DuBois","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MMD1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-14T12:17:25.0166667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H4408/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":null,"DocumentText":"\t(a) There shall be a task force to reassess school integration within the Metropolitan Council for Educational Opportunity program, hereinafter called the METCO program. \r\n\tThe task force shall consist of 13 members: 2 of whom shall be the chairs of the joint committee on education or their designees, who shall serve as co-chairs; 1 of whom shall be appointed by the speaker of the house of representatives or a designee; 1 of whom shall be appointed by the president of the senate or a designee; 1 of whom shall be the minority leader of the house of representatives or a designee; 1 of whom shall be the minority leader of the senate or a designee; 1 of whom shall be the secretary of education or a designee; 1 of whom shall be the commissioner of elementary and secondary education or a designee; 1 of whom shall be the president of the Black Educators Alliance of Massachusetts, Inc. or a designee; 1 of whom shall be the president of the National Association for the Advancement of Colored People New England Area Conference or a designee; and 3 of whom shall be appointed by the governor and shall be former participants in the METCO program. \r\n\tThe task force shall evaluate the historical impact of the METCO program in the commonwealth and make recommendations to the general court regarding school integration and improvements to the program.  \r\n\t(b) The task force shall convene beginning not later than 180 days after the effective date of this act and meet not fewer than 4 times. The task force shall submit its findings and recommendations, including any proposed legislation, by filing the same with the clerks of the house of representatives and senate and the governor not later than 1 year after the effective date of this act\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Redraft","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}